+# CampusIQ
+
+**AI-powered campus operations command center** — a privacy-first digital twin for live occupancy, classroom availability, event crowds, campus facilities, parking, safety alerts and historical trends.
+
+> **Demo data notice:** The default workspace is a fictional, self-contained demo. All people, events, readings, cameras and alert scenarios are synthetic. The dashboard is designed to work without real CCTV hardware.
+
+## What works in this MVP
+
+- A real React + TypeScript command center with 13 interactive workspace areas: overview, camera monitoring, campus digital twin, classrooms, events, parking, facilities, analytics, alerts, assistant, resources, system health and privacy settings.
+- FastAPI APIs, relational SQLAlchemy models, SQLite for a no-setup demo and PostgreSQL for Docker deployments.
+- Short-lived signed HS256 bearer sessions, four role types, permission checks on write routes, institution-account password hashing and a one-click passwordless demo sign-in.
+- A five-second WebSocket live snapshot and API-side demo simulator for anonymous population, room, event, vehicle, camera and parking updates. WebSocket reconnect plus HTTP refresh fallback are included.
+- Camera management for simulated feeds, backend-configured RTSP sources and uploaded/pre-recorded video. RTSP source URLs are Fernet-encrypted in the database and never returned by the API. Video uploads and live RTSP feeds are sampled at a configurable low rate for efficient anonymous counting; uploaded source clips are processed in temporary storage and discarded after analysis.
+- A local OpenCV HOG detector fallback and an optional separate inference service. Configure an institution-supplied YOLO weights file using `YOLO_MODEL_PATH` to enable YOLO inference. No face recognition, biometric templates, identity tracking, plate recognition or individual attendance records are part of CampusIQ.
+- Working event CRUD, crowd-threshold alerts, alert acknowledgement/resolution/ignore, individually stateful parking slots, resource status updates, role management, privacy/retention controls, CSV analytics export and a local campus-data assistant.
+- Responsive desktop/tablet/mobile layout, charts, interactive SVG campus plan, demo camera scenes, status indicators, browser notifications and user-friendly error/reconnect states.
+
+## Demo flow
+
+1. Start the API and frontend using the instructions below, or run `docker compose up --build`.
+2. Open the frontend. On first visit, CampusIQ opens a **SUPER ADMIN** demo session automatically; use the profile menu to sign out and select another role.
+3. Review the live population and current campus signals on **Campus overview**.
+4. Open **Camera monitoring** to view five simulated feeds and a sixth offline-camera scenario. Toggle a feed or anonymous AI counting, upload a short video, or add a demo/RTSP source.
+5. Open **Events & venues** and select **Trigger warning** to set an event crowd above 90% and generate a live capacity alert.
+6. Inspect the **Smart parking** slot grid. In an authorized role, clicking a slot rotates it through available, occupied, reserved and disabled states.
+7. Check **Classrooms**, then ask the **Campus assistant**: “Which classrooms are available for 50 students?” The local API answers from current room records.
+8. Explore the **Digital twin**, **Analytics & reports**, **Alert center**, and **System health**.
+
+## Local installation
+
+Requirements: Python 3.11+, Node.js 20+, npm 9+.
+
+### 1. Start the backend
+
+```bash
+cd backend
+python3 -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate           # Windows: .venv\\Scripts\\activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
+```
+
+The API seeds fictional campus data into `backend/campusiq.db` on first start. No database server, model weights, camera or external AI account is required for demo mode. API docs: [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs).
+
+RTSP source URLs are encrypted before database storage with a Fernet key derived from `CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY`. The built-in key is only for a private local demo. Before adding real camera sources, set a strong secret and keep it stable across restarts; changing it makes previously stored RTSP sources unreadable. Never put this key or camera credentials in frontend configuration.
+
+### 2. Start the frontend in another terminal
+
+```bash
+cd frontend
+npm install
+npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173
+```
+
+Open [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173). Vite proxies same-origin `/api` and `/ws` to port 8000; browser code never calls `localhost` as a separate service.
+
+### Optional local OpenCV / YOLO setup
+
+`backend/requirements.txt` installs OpenCV for frame sampling and an OpenCV HOG person-counting fallback. YOLO is optional and intentionally has no bundled weights. Install a compatible `ultralytics` version separately, provide approved weights with `YOLO_MODEL_PATH`, and review model-license and institutional/privacy obligations before enabling it. Counts and aggregate detections only are retained.
+
+## PostgreSQL + isolated AI worker (Docker Compose)
+
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env
+# For a real deployment, use a generated, stable secret and unique DB password.
+python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"  # set as CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY in .env
+docker compose up --build
+```
+
+- Frontend: `http://localhost:5173`
+- Backend/OpenAPI: `http://localhost:8000/docs`
+- PostgreSQL: `localhost:5432`
+- Separate AI inference health: `http://localhost:8100/health` inside the Compose network
+
+Compose configures PostgreSQL, a standalone AI inference container and an internal API-to-AI URL. If the AI worker is unavailable, video/image analysis falls back to the backend’s local OpenCV engine. Change all development secrets, disable `CAMPUSIQ_DEMO_MODE`, provision an institution account and use TLS/managed identity before production.
+
+The default Docker Compose password is **for local development only**. Do not reuse it or the example secret in a deployed system.
+
+## Authentication and roles
+
+The first run auto-opens the sample workspace for an easy hackathon demo. The secure sign-in screen is available from **Profile → Sign out**. Choose a role under **Demo workspace** (no password is stored), or configure an institution account with environment variables:
+
+```env
+ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@your-campus.edu
+ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-unique-password
+CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY=use-a-long-random-secret
+CAMPUSIQ_DEMO_MODE=false
+```
+
+On first database initialization, the configured institution account password is PBKDF2-hashed. Do not put production secrets in frontend environment variables. Role checks are enforced by the backend: Super Admin, Campus Admin, Security Admin and Event Admin have different write capabilities. Demo identities are synthetic and are not real accounts.
+
+> For an existing development DB, account bootstrap values are applied at first seed. Reset the ignored local SQLite file only when intentionally reseeding local demo data. PostgreSQL production changes should use migrations and institution identity provisioning.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```text
+RTSP source / uploaded clip / demo feed
+              ↓
+optional isolated AI service (YOLO weights) or local OpenCV fallback
+              ↓
+anonymous person / vehicle counts · sampled frames, no identities
+              ↓
+FastAPI + role-checked REST + local campus-data assistant
+              ↓
+PostgreSQL (Docker) / SQLite (local demo)
+              ↓
+React dashboard ← WebSocket five-second snapshots + reconnect/poll fallback
+              ↓
+Digital twin · occupancy · parking · alerts · analytics · reports
+```
+
+Detailed system diagram and service boundaries: [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md). Database entities: [`database/schema.md`](database/schema.md). REST/WebSocket endpoints: [`docs/api.md`](docs/api.md).
+
+## Project layout
+
+```text
+frontend/         React + TypeScript + Vite UI, charts and same-origin API client
+backend/app/      FastAPI routes, signed auth, simulator, data models and local DB
+ai_service/       Optional separately deployed OpenCV/YOLO inference worker
+database/         Schema and data-governance notes
+docs/             Architecture and API documentation
+docker-compose.yml PostgreSQL + backend + AI worker + responsive web app
+```
+
+## Tests and production notes
+
+```bash
+# Frontend type-check and production bundle
+cd frontend && npm run build
+
+# Backend tests
+cd backend
+pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
+.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
+```
+
+SQLite is a lightweight local/demo mode; Docker Compose is the PostgreSQL execution path. SQLAlchemy creates the MVP schema at startup. RTSP source URIs are Fernet-encrypted at the application layer; a stable, high-entropy `CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY` is required to decrypt them. The privacy retention control currently records an administrator-selected policy value—it does not run an automated purge job. The privacy-masking toggle is also a stored policy preference; this MVP does not display camera frames or apply image masks. Before a university deployment, add Alembic migrations, institution-managed SSO, full database/storage encryption, rate limiting, monitoring, backups, verified deletion, automated retention enforcement and masking in any production video display pipeline. Establish access controls, campus-specific network/video-retention controls, notice/consent practices and a documented incident process. Review applicable law and institutional policy before connecting real camera feeds. Use anonymous aggregate counts only; facial recognition and identity tracking are not supported.
