@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# CampusIQ API reference
+
+FastAPI also publishes an interactive OpenAPI specification at `http://localhost:8000/docs` and JSON schema at `/openapi.json`. Except for `/`, `/api`, `/api/auth/demo`, and `/api/auth/login`, HTTP API routes require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. The live WebSocket requires an authenticated bearer token in its subprotocols (see below).
+
+## Authentication and operations
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST` | `/api/auth/demo` | Create a passwordless, role-selected demonstration session. |
+| `POST` | `/api/auth/login` | Sign in with a configured institution account. |
+| `GET` | `/api/auth/me` | Resolve the current session. |
+| `POST` | `/api/auth/password` | Change an institution account password (12-character minimum). |
+| `GET` | `/api/dashboard`, `/api/snapshot` | Current aggregate command-center snapshot. |
+| `GET` | `/api/buildings`, `/api/buildings/{id}`, `/api/floors` | Digital twin and floor detail. |
+| `GET` | `/api/rooms`, `/api/classrooms`, `/api/timetables` | Room inventory and schedules. |
+| `GET` | `/api/occupancy` | Building/floor occupancy aggregates and density labels. |
+| `GET` | `/api/cameras` | Camera status with source credentials redacted. |
+| `POST` | `/api/cameras` | Add a demo or RTSP source (Super Admin / Security Admin). |
+| `PATCH`, `DELETE` | `/api/cameras/{id}` | Update stream / AI state or remove a camera. |
+| `POST` | `/api/cameras/{id}/test` | Test a demo connection or sample one frame from the RTSP source using the backend decoder. |
+| `POST` | `/api/cameras/{id}/upload` | Analyze sampled video frames from temporary storage; the original clip is discarded after processing. Only aggregate results are retained. |
+| `GET` | `/api/detections?camera_id=CAM-001&limit=50` | Anonymous camera-event aggregates (maximum 500). |
+| `POST` | `/api/detections/ingest` | Ingest aggregate people/vehicle counts for a camera (Super Admin / Security Admin). No image or identity fields are accepted. |
+| `POST` | `/api/vision/analyze-image` | Optional anonymous image inference; submitted pixels are processed and not persisted. |
+| `GET` | `/api/parking` | Parking zones, slot state and usage chart series. |
+| `GET` | `/api/vehicles?period=24h\|7d\|30d` | Aggregate vehicle totals by zone and time; no plates or identifiers. |
+| `PATCH` | `/api/parking/slots/{id}` | Change a slot to available, occupied, reserved or disabled. |
+| `GET` | `/api/events` | Venue crowd and schedule data. |
+| `POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` | `/api/events` and `/api/events/{id}` | Event management (Campus / Event Admin). |
+| `POST` | `/api/events/{id}/simulate-spike` | Set a demo event to a high crowd threshold and create an alert. |
+| `GET`, `PATCH` | `/api/alerts` and `/api/alerts/{id}` | List, filter, acknowledge, resolve or ignore alerts. |
+| `POST` | `/api/alerts/test` | Generate a local restricted-area test alert. |
+| `GET` | `/api/restricted-zones` | Restricted-zone polygons and enable state. |
+| `POST`, `PATCH` | `/api/restricted-zones` and `/api/restricted-zones/{id}` | Configure restricted polygons (normalized frame coordinates). |
+| `POST` | `/api/restricted-zones/{id}/simulate-entry` | Demonstrate restricted-zone alerting. |
+| `GET` | `/api/facilities`, `/api/resources` | Current shared-space occupancy and asset state. |
+| `PATCH` | `/api/resources/{id}` | Update shared resource availability. |
+| `GET` | `/api/analytics?period=24h\|yesterday\|7d\|30d` | Population, utilization, parking and camera trends. Optional `start` and `end` support custom ranges. |
+| `GET` | `/api/analytics/export?period=7d` | Download CSV (PDF via browser print). |
+| `POST` | `/api/assistant/ask` | Ask a question grounded in the current API database. |
+| `GET`, `PATCH` | `/api/settings` | Privacy, retention and demo settings. |
+| `GET` | `/api/users` | Role roster (Super Admin only). |
+| `PATCH` | `/api/users/{id}/role` | Change a configured role (Super Admin only). |
+| `GET` | `/api/system/health` | Backend, database, AI, camera, WebSocket and simulator health. |
+| `POST` | `/api/demo/toggle` | Pause/resume synthetic live data (Super / Campus Admin). |
+
+## Detection-ingest payload
+
+`POST /api/detections/ingest` accepts aggregate values only:
+
+```json
+{
+  "camera_id": "CAM-001",
+  "people_count": 12,
+  "vehicle_count": 3,
+  "confidence": 0.86,
+  "event_type": "ANONYMOUS_COUNT"
+}
+```
+
+The backend stores counts, confidence, event type and a timestamp, updates the camera/parking aggregates and may emit a location-level alert for a configured restricted zone. Upload clips are written to temporary storage only while analysis runs and are deleted after the request; the endpoint does not persist frames, faces, license plates, individual IDs or identity tracks.
+
+## Privacy and deployment notes
+
+RTSP source URLs are encrypted at rest with Fernet using a key derived from `CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY`. The key is not returned by the API and must remain stable to decrypt existing sources. Camera create/update payloads may include `source_uri`, but camera responses intentionally omit it. Store deployment keys outside source control and never put them in frontend variables.
+
+`GET`/`PATCH /api/settings` expose retention/privacy preferences; the retention-days value is not an automated purge, and the privacy-masking flag is a stored policy preference rather than an active frame-masking pipeline in this MVP. Establish the institution's legal basis, notice/consent process, access-control policy and retention schedule before connecting real camera feeds, then implement and verify automated deletion and masking appropriate to that policy. This product does not provide facial recognition or identity tracking.
+
+## WebSocket
+
+Connect to `/ws/live` with `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: campusiq, bearer.<accessToken>`. CampusIQ accepts the `campusiq` subprotocol; the bearer token is sent in the WebSocket handshake, not the URL. Do not log this protocol header. For example, browser clients may use `new WebSocket(relativeWsUrl, ['campusiq', 'bearer.' + token])`. Unauthenticated or expired sessions are rejected.
+
+The first frame and every five-second update look like:
+
+```json
+{ "type": "snapshot", "payload": { "timestamp": "…", "metrics": { "population": 4170 }, "buildings": [], "alerts": [] } }
+```
+
+The client should reconnect on close. Data is an operational estimate; it is not suitable as an individual attendance record.
