@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# CampusIQ architecture
+
+## System flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  A[RTSP cameras / uploaded clips] --> B[AI inference worker]
+  D[Demo feed simulator] --> B
+  B --> C[Anonymous person + vehicle counts]
+  C --> E[FastAPI service]
+  E --> F[(PostgreSQL / local SQLite)]
+  E --> G[REST API]
+  E --> H[WebSocket live snapshot]
+  G --> I[React + TypeScript dashboard]
+  H --> I
+  I --> J[Alerts + charts + digital twin]
+  I --> K[Local campus assistant]
+```
+
+## Services
+
+- **Frontend:** React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind utilities, custom enterprise UI components, Recharts and Lucide. It uses relative `/api` and `/ws` URLs; Vite proxies both to the API, including in Arena preview.
+- **Backend:** FastAPI, Pydantic and SQLAlchemy. JWT-style signed bearer sessions, role checks, event CRUD, alert actions, parking slot operations, CSV reports, upload handling and OpenAPI docs (`/docs`).
+- **Storage:** PostgreSQL in Docker Compose. SQLite is the local fallback for a frictionless demo. Historical aggregates and operational records are persisted.
+- **AI:** An optional standalone FastAPI inference service (`ai_service/`) and a local OpenCV fallback. It can use an institution-supplied YOLO model path; otherwise an OpenCV HOG person detector is used. Video frames are sampled (default ~1 fps) and resized before inference; live RTSP sampling reads one frame at a time. Only counts, confidence and event metadata are stored. No faces, embeddings, license plates or identity tracks are produced.
+- **Realtime:** Backend simulator updates campus state and broadcasts a bounded snapshot over WebSocket every five seconds. The frontend reconnects automatically and retains a polling fallback.
+- **Demo mode:** No CCTV is required. Synthetic campus population, room occupancy, camera state, vehicle counts, event crowd size and parking slots evolve on the API side. Simulated camera panels are explicitly labelled.
+
+## Boundaries and deployment
+
+The AI worker may run separately from the API using `AI_SERVICE_URL`. If it is unavailable, API uploads fall back to the local OpenCV processor. RTSP source URIs are accepted only by the backend, Fernet-encrypted before database storage with a key derived from `CAMPUSIQ_SECRET_KEY`, and omitted from camera, dashboard and health responses. Keep that secret stable: rotating it without re-encrypting stored sources makes them unreadable. Frontend routes never contact a user's `localhost`; they call same-origin relative paths.
+
+The privacy retention control is a policy preference only; this MVP does not run a scheduled purge. Before production use, add automated retention enforcement, HTTPS, a unique high-entropy stable key, full database/storage encryption, private network access to camera feeds, institution-managed authentication, access reviews, camera notices/consent, a documented retention schedule and tested deletion/export workflows. Review applicable law and institutional policy with campus privacy and legal teams. Do not enable identity tracking or facial recognition.
